==German==
===Etymology===
''[[ost]] + [[Deutschland]]''<br>
East Germany. While geographically not completely accurate (some parts of the former West Germany are located further east than parts of the former East Germany), this term is frequently used to distinguish the region formerly known as "East Germany" or German Democratic Republic (Deutsche Demokratische Republik) from the former "West Germany" or Federal Republic of Germany (Bundesrepublik Deutschland), which were two separate nations from 1949 until they were reunified in 1990 as the Federal Republic of Germany.

===Noun===
'''Ostdeutschland''' ''n''
# [[East Germany]], the former German Democratic Republic
